{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.html#Lean.Markdown.parseDocument\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Markdown</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseDocument</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/String/Defs.html#String.Slice\">String.Slice</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">indent</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> := <span class=\"fn\">0</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">extensions</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions\">Extensions</a> := <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions.mk\">{</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions.mk\">}</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">externalRefs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Data/HashMap/Basic.html#Std.HashMap\">Std.HashMap</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.ExternalRef\">ExternalRef</a></span> := <a href=\"./Init/Core.html#EmptyCollection.emptyCollection\">∅</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.Block\">Block</a> <span class=\"fn\">s</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses `s` as a Markdown document.\n\nUp to `indent` leading spaces of each line are skipped.\n\nBy default, the parser adheres to CommonMark with one exception. It compares link labels modulo\nUnicode case folding only for the Latin-1 and Greek ranges, while CommonMark specifies full Unicode\ncase folding. Use `extensions` to enable non-standard extensions like LaTeX math.\n\nThe `externalRefs` table maps labels to reference definitions beyond the document's own link\nreference definitions. Its labels are normalized like those in the document, and when several of\nthem normalize to the same label, the definition of the lexicographically least of them is used. A\nreference definition in the document takes precedence over an external definition with the same\nlabel unless the external definition has `overrideDocument` set.\n\nThis parser is based on the two-pass algorithm described in the CommonMark specification.","docLink":"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.html#Lean.Markdown.parseDocument","kind":"def","line":51,"name":"Lean.Markdown.parseDocument","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.lean#L51-L72"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">partial def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.html#Lean.Markdown.parseInlinesInBlock\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Markdown</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseInlinesInBlock</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/String/Defs.html#String.Slice\">String.Slice</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">refs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.RefTable\">RefTable</a> <span class=\"fn\">s</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">block</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.Block.Raw\">Block.Raw</a> <span class=\"fn\">s</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">extensions</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions\">Extensions</a> := <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions.mk\">{</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Inline.html#Lean.Markdown.Extensions.mk\">}</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.Block\">Block</a> <span class=\"fn\">s</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses the inline content of a block from the first pass, with `refs` set to the document's link\nreference definitions. This is the second pass of the algorithm described in the CommonMark\nspecification.\n\nTwo passes are necessary because the presence of a link definition later in the document affects the\nsyntactic interpretation of reference-style links earlier in the document.","docLink":"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.html#Lean.Markdown.parseInlinesInBlock","kind":"opaque","line":17,"name":"Lean.Markdown.parseInlinesInBlock","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/Markdown/Parser.lean#L17-L49"}}],"imports":["Lean.Data.Markdown.Parser.Block","Lean.Data.Markdown.Parser.Inline"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Data.Markdown.Parser"}